#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""local-llm-api-proxy - serve the llama.cpp web UI on 127.0.0.1:8080, but answer
chats with a cloud API model (Local LLM Menu -> Run via API).

Started by start-local-llm when the active model is "api:<provider>:<variant>"
(providers live in ~/.config/local-llm/api-providers.json). The web UI, Ellama
and anything else keep using http://127.0.0.1:8080 unchanged.

Security:
  * listens on 127.0.0.1 only and rejects requests whose Host header is not
    127.0.0.1/localhost (blocks DNS-rebinding attacks from web pages)
  * CORS answers only localhost origins
  * requires the same API key as llama-server (secrets/llama-server.key) for
    everything except UI files, /health and /v1/models
  * the provider's API key is read per request from secrets/<provider>/...,
    sent only to that provider's base_url (HTTPS required unless loopback),
    and never logged or returned
  * web tools (/tools, same contract as llama-server) run in the bwrap sandbox
    via local-llm-mcp-run, and the web UI asks before every tool call
"""
